<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Presian I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 836–852</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Presian I was ruler (khan) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a> from 836 to 852. During his reign <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> expanded into Macedonia, taking the lands of Slavic tribes such as the Smolyani after their revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> in 837, and fought a war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> of Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlastimir">Vlastimir</a> that ended in Bulgarian defeat. He was succeeded by Boris I, under whom Bulgaria converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/presian-i.jpg" alt="Presian I" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Lefterov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philippi_Inscription_1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
